0.1370.19 claim 17 stands rejected under 35 U.S.C. § 103 as allegedly beingunpatentable over Pan in view of Chua, Eichler, and U.S. Patent Application Publication No. 2015/0072889 to Lui et al.; claim 18 stands rejected under 35 U.S.C. § 103 as allegedly being unpatentable over Pan in view of Chua and U.S. Patent No. 5,465,728 to Phillips; and claims 19- 21 stand rejected under 35 U.S.C. § 103 as allegedly being unpatentable over Pan in view of Chua and U.S. Patent Application Publication No. 2004/0138577 to Kline.

The Official Action then takes check valve (123), which is disposed in the collection branch (109) as corresponding to the recited air diverter, which divides the sample delivery part into an upstream portion and a downstream portion. This is problematic because Pan explicitly provides that check valve (123) permits the breath sample to flow through the branch and into the container(117), but inhibits withdrawal of gas or liquid from the container upon inhalation SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.0970.113 the orientationof check valve (123) permits the breath sample to flow outwardly from the mouthpiece end (111) through the tube (107), sample collection branch (109) and to block air flow through the sample collection branch, container and tube toward the mouthpiece end (Pan at para. [0064]). Since the check valve (123) blocks air from flowing back through the sample collection branch (109), Pan lacks a sample outlet in the upstream portion.
